Experiment 1: Create Maven Build Pipeline in Azure
Aim: To create and execute a Maven build pipeline using Azure DevOps.

Software needed: IntelliJ IDEA, Java JDK 17, Maven, Git, GitHub and Azure DevOps.
Steps to perform
1. Open Azure DevOps and sign in.
2. Create a new project and select Private visibility.
3. Open IntelliJ IDEA → New Project → Java → Maven.
4. Select JDK 17, enter a project name and click Create.
5. Create Main.java inside src/main/java and write the Java program.
6. Open the IntelliJ terminal and compile the project:
   mvn compile
   mvn package
7. Create a new repository on GitHub.
8. Push your project to GitHub using:
   git init
   git add .
   git commit -m "First Commit"
   git branch -M main
   git remote add origin YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL
   git push -u origin main
9. Return to Azure DevOps → Pipelines → New Pipeline.
10. Select GitHub as the source and authorize access.
11. Select your GitHub repository.
12. Choose the Maven pipeline configuration.
13. Azure generates the azure-pipelines.yml file based on your Maven project.
14. Set the JDK version to 17 in the YAML configuration.
15. Click Save and Run.
16. Open Jobs and check the build output.
